FYI:

I downloaded the absurd tiles 64x64 bitmap set (drop dead gorgeous, but
the creator could have skipped the visual pun on "grid bug", though it
is funny) and attempted to use it in the current 3.4.3 NetHackW GUI
version under MS-Windows 98 second edition, with an appropriate
defaults.nh entry
like:

The game told me it couldn't open the picture file, and reverted to the
default small tiles.

I confirmed that the file was readable by both GIMP 1.2.5 and Mozilla
1.6 beta (though not by the buggy image viewer that comes out of the box
in 98SE), saved a copy from the GIMP to see if using a different *.bmp
encoder would make the image file usable, but no joy.

However, by scaling the image to the sizes appropriate for 32x32 and
48x48 tiles, and making the obvious changes to the OPTIONS line, I was
able to play the game at either of those sizes, though with a loss of
image quality; still Absurd at 48x48 is Pretty Darn Nice.

I found a second minor problem at the 48x48 size; the travel command as
given by a mouse click uses the wrong scaling and overshoots the
intended target grid square to land at one multiple (3x?) times further
away.  I didn't think to test that with the 32x32 set.

This problem has been reported to the DevTeam using the "form fillout"
"comments" dialog, (since I couldn't immediately locate the bugzilla
URL) under sequence number #U816; I'm just reporting it here as both
information and a hint for any clue how to make the 64x64 Absurd tile
size work in 3.4.3 someone else may have acquired.  Win 98SE is pretty
dusty, this may be an OS dependent bug, as well.

I'm just naturally itching to try the 72x72, 96x96, and 128x128 (legally
blind NetHacker player version) Absurd tiles as well, but so far
progress has been downward in tile size from the ones available, The
Wrong Direction.

